API.md M5, API.md M6, API.md E11: renaming a table key shorter renames each ref to it, map keys
included; a key whose value is a `[ ]` list written `key: [` with only its brackets broken
(FORMATTER.md §7.2 rule A) lets the list lay flat once the shorter key leaves room, whether the
key is a bare name or a string. Every byte outside the items re-printed is kept.
-- options --
pkgs: p
